title: The Social Democrats
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_spd_timer <= 0 and time >= 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_spd_timer = 4;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.c_spd_answer = 0;
!}
frequency: 250
is-card: true
tags: germany

= The Social Democrats

[? if year = 1919 : The SPD governs. Ebert, Scheidemann and Noske sent the Freikorps against the workers of Berlin. Millions of workers still vote for it, and many of them are ashamed. ?][? if year >= 1920 and year <= 1921 : The SPD is still the largest workers' party in Germany, and its unions hold the factories. Its members are tired of governing with the bourgeois parties for nothing. ?][? if year >= 1922 : The SPD is the party of the Republic and of eight million trade unionists. Its leaders fear us more than the right, and its members are not sure they agree. ?]

- @offer: Offer the SPD joint action on wages and against the right.
- @below: Appeal to its members over the heads of their leaders.
- @expose: Print the record of the SPD leaders.
- @easy_discard

@offer
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] [? if spd_in_government = 1 : While they sit in the cabinet, the leaders are likely to refuse. ?][? if spd_in_government = 0 : Out of office, they may accept. ?]
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
var p = Q.spd_in_government ? 0.2 : 0.55;
if (Math.random() < p) {
    Q.c_spd_answer = 1;
    Q.spd_relation += 12;
    Q.worker_support += 4;
    RG.news('SPD and Communists agree on joint action', 2);
} else {
    Q.c_spd_answer = 2;
    Q.spd_relation += 3;
}
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

[? if c_spd_answer = 1 : The SPD executive accepts, to everyone's surprise, its own included. Joint meetings are called in every big town. ?][? if c_spd_answer = 2 : The SPD executive refuses. Several of its local branches accept anyway. ?]

@below
subtitle: A few hundred social democrats come over. Their leaders are furious.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spd_relation -= 4;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.03;
}
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our leaflets at the SPD's own meetings ask its members why their ministers sit with the industrialists.

@expose
subtitle: The bridges burn. The SPD's workers feel insulted too.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spd_relation -= 10;
Q.militancy += 5;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Die Rote Fahne prints the names of the workers shot by the Freikorps, and beside them the name of the minister who signed the order.
